# AskmeHUMG – Project Context

## What is this app?
Anonymous Q&A mobile app for HUMG university students. Anyone can send anonymous questions to a registered student (Host). Hosts answer and optionally publish replies to a public Feed.

## Tech Stack
- **Flutter** (Dart) – UI framework
- **Riverpod** (`flutter_riverpod`) – State management
- **Firebase Auth** – Google Sign-In (any Google account); HUMG email verified separately via OTP (UC-1.3)
- **Cloud Firestore** – NoSQL database
- **Firebase Storage** – Avatar and media storage
- **Cloud Functions** – Rate limiting, server-side moderation (OTP is client-generated, not via Cloud Function)
- **Firebase App Check** – Bot protection for anonymous question submission
- **`app_links`** – Deep links (`askme-humg-app.web.app/user/{userId}`)

## User Roles
- **Anonymous Sender** – No login required, sends questions via deep link
- **Host** – Logged-in user with verified `@humg.edu.vn` email (`isHumgVerified: true`)
- **Viewer** – Browses public Feed (guest or logged-in)
- **Admin** – Firebase Custom Claim `admin: true`

## Key Business Rules
1. Any Google account can sign in; Host features unlock only after OTP-verifying a `@humg.edu.vn` email
2. Anonymous questions: max 300 chars, rate-limited at 5/device/hour via App Check + Cloud Functions
3. Likes: one per user per answer (enforced via `likedBy`; server keeps `likeCount` in sync)
4. Answers → Batch Write updating both `answers` and `questions` (UC-3.3)
5. Comments → Transaction: `comments` + `answers.commentCount` + `hotScore` (UC-4.3)
6. No direct messaging or real-time chat

## Firestore Collections
- `users`: uid, name, avatar, email, role, createdAt, isBlocked, isHumgVerified, humgEmail
- `questions`: questionId, toUserId, content, createdAt, status (`unanswered`|`answered`)
- `answers`: answerId, questionId, userId, content, createdAt, likeCount, likedBy[], isPublished, commentCount, `hotScore` (trending), **hostName**, **hostAvatar**, **hostIsHumgVerified** (denormalized for feed display)
- `comments`: commentId, answerId, userId (nullable), content, isAnonymous, createdAt, **authorName**, **authorAvatar**, **authorIsHumgVerified** (denormalized for display)
- `reports`: reportId, targetId, targetType, reportedBy, reason, status, createdAt, resolvedAt
- `otpRequests`: email, otpHash, expiresAt, attempts

## Verified Badge
- Widget: `lib/app/global_widgets/ui/verified_badge.dart` (`VerifiedBadge`)
- Two modes: `inline: true` (icon only, for name rows), `inline: false` (icon + "HUMG" label, for profile header)
- Shown wherever `isHumgVerified / hostIsHumgVerified / authorIsHumgVerified == true`
- Locations: ProfileHeader (next to name + subtitle row), FeedItemCard (next to host name), CommentTile (next to author name, hidden for anonymous)

## Feed Interaction Rules
- **Default feed sort:** `hotScore` descending (trending). App may temporarily fall back to `createdAt` if the trending composite index is building or the query fails.
- **View feed**: open to all (guest, logged-in, unverified)
- **Like / Comment**: requires `isHumgVerified == true`; unverified users see a snackbar directing them to verify
- Guard implemented via `BuildContextX.requireVerified()` in `lib/app/core/extensions/context_extensions.dart`
- Snackbar keys: `verifyRequiredToLike`, `verifyRequiredToComment`

## OTP / HUMG Verification (UC-1.3)
- Email sending: Gmail SMTP via `mailer` package, plain-text body (HTML blocked by HUMG Microsoft 365 filter)
- Env vars: `GMAIL_USER`, `GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD` (Gmail App Password, 2FA required)
- OTP: 6-digit secure random, SHA-256 hashed, stored in `otpRequests/{uid}`
- Expiry: 10 minutes, max 3 wrong attempts before lockout
- Route guard: unverified users → `/verify-humg` (except `/` feed which is skippable)
